<title>UK: No plans to raise mortgage rates -Woolwich.</title>
<headline>No plans to raise mortgage rates -Woolwich.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Woolwich Building Society said on Wednesday it had no plans to raise mortgage rates following the Bank of England's decision earlier to raise the minimum lending rate by a quarter-point to six percent.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no plans to raise rates,&quot; a Woolwich spokesman said. &quot;In view of the improving housing market we would be reluctant to increase mortgagge rates and we will remain competitive on both savings and mortgage products,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 71 542 7717</p>
</text>
